# AGENTS.md — miToosa

This codebase uses the **AgToosa** framework. Read `Docs/AgToosa_Agent.md` before beginning any task.

## Project

**miToosa** — cross-platform Flutter puzzle game (iOS, Android, macOS, Web). ADHD-optimized gameplay loop. Local-first, anonymous auth, encrypted Hive storage, Riverpod state management.

## Source of Truth

- `Docs/Master-Plan.md` — project state, Epics, active sprint, backlog
- `Docs/Context/` — product.md, tech-stack.md, workflow.md, product-guidelines.md
- `Docs/AgToosa_Changelog.md` — project changelog

## Core Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `/agtoosa-spec` | Research, specify, and architect a feature |
| `/agtoosa-build` | Implement with TDD (Red-Green-Refactor) |
| `/agtoosa-qa` | QA planning, execution, defect triage |
| `/agtoosa-review` | Security, architecture, and cross-platform review |
| `/agtoosa-ship` | Pre-ship checklist, docs sync, retro |

Sub-commands: append `research`, `plan`, `quick` (spec) · `scope`, `tdd`, `test` (build) · `plan`, `run`, `report`, `triage` (qa) · `security`, `arch`, `debug`, `cross` (review) · `check`, `docs`, `retro` (ship).

## Key Rules

- TDD is enforced — write failing tests before implementation (Red-Green-Refactor).
- Run `dart analyze` and `flutter test` before every commit.
- Run `dart pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs` after modifying Riverpod providers.
- Keep `Docs/Master-Plan.md` updated after every phase transition.
- Do not modify `docs/PRODUCT-WEDGE.md` without explicit user approval — it is the canonical product economy reference.

## Architecture

Three layers — never mix concerns:
1. `lib/core/engine/` — pure Dart game engines (no Flutter, no Hive)
2. `lib/features/` — Riverpod StateNotifiers connecting engines to UI
3. `lib/data/` — encrypted Hive persistence and telemetry

## Verification Gates

```bash
dart analyze
flutter test
flutter pub get
dart pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs  # after provider changes
```
